{"skill":{"slug":"qq-zone-photo","displayName":"Qq Zone Photo"},"version":{"version":"1.0.3","createdAt":1773542653366,"changelog":"- Skill 名称从 \"qq-zone-photo-skills\" 修改为 \"qq-zone-photo\"。\n- 更新并简化了 README 和说明文档表述。\n- 明确 skill 描述及 metadata 信息，使表述更简洁一致。\n- 无新增功能或接口变更，仅文档和元数据调整。","changelogSource":"auto","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"README.md","size":3154,"sha256":"537ce2325db5eada3015364ad66069e568a8caa19f296256d41204705a668271","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3481,"sha256":"503180dda8a19ac617269557363e32feeb63b03f2468049c6c6fce54c8d18d27","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"_meta.json","size":209,"sha256":"f47ceb37b57041c13f71410773c938b9abd93a5a2cc6b153640ad9a28f87411c","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"requirements.txt","size":67,"sha256":"4b296ac1ffb78d100e0f60e9ed34bbea4a93794ed8108863c321c7a19634d630","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"scripts/qzone_photos.py","size":27379,"sha256":"67a04f74ff2ac5adb2396ea3b0c0f589794528c2a3048d71fd661114d414491f","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2270,"sha256":"8917999dd1433e898582e8b07cf2efa2eeaff5b806e8e345dfccc68ec5d0f967","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789177161414,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"4ba6b6d9594b7ff28fd4a3770942765120e672b373606a5472ca505c27de62ab","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/4ba6b6d9594b7ff28fd4a3770942765120e672b373606a5472ca505c27de62ab","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086056666},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":81,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":16,"checkedAt":1789177161414},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill does what it claims for QQ Zone photo management, but it handles account cookies and downloads in ways that deserve careful review before installation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access and local photo file access are purpose-aligned, but unvalidated URLs, unsanitized remote filenames, unrestricted output paths, and a fixed temporary QR file broaden the local and network impact beyond the intended QQ photo workflow.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No hidden installer, startup hook, or persistence mechanism was found, but dependencies are specified with lower bounds rather than exact pinned versions.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The usage instructions disclose shell-based CLI actions and cookie use, but they do not set clear guardrails for arbitrary download URLs, public album creation, credential output, or confirmation before high-impact account and file operations.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill stores active QQ session cookies in plaintext JSON using ambient file permissions and prints the login result, including sensitive session values, to stdout; no logout or cookie removal workflow is provided.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"QR login, album listing, photo upload/download, and album creation match the stated purpose, but the implementation also permits arbitrary URL downloads through an authenticated session and creates albums as public without a documented visibility choice.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable giving the skill QQ Zone session access and letting it read/write local photo files. Use a dedicated cookies file with restrictive permissions, avoid running it on shared systems, do not pass untrusted download URLs, review album visibility after creation, and remove the cookie file when finished.","findings":"[LP3] expected: Shell execution plus local file and network access are expected for this CLI-based photo manager, but the artifact does not narrow those capabilities for sensitive account and filesystem operations.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-only documentation is coherent with a QQ Zone utility and is not treated as a security escalation by itself.\n[SQP-2] unexpected: Persisting cookies is expected for login reuse, but plaintext storage without explicit restrictive permissions and printing session values to stdout are under-protected for active account credentials.\n[AST4] expected: The subprocess calls only open the locally saved QR image with fixed argument lists, so this finding is downgraded as expected QR-display behavior rather than command-injection evidence.\n[SQP-2] expected: Uploading a chosen local photo and sending session authentication to QQ endpoints is core functionality, though the user-facing text should be clearer about what is transmitted during upload.\n[SDI-2] unexpected: The single-photo download action accepts any URL and fetches it with the authenticated session, which is broader than a QQ Zone photo-management purpose requires.\n[SC1] unexpected: Unpinned dependencies are not malicious, but they reduce reproducibility for a skill that processes images and authenticated network requests.\n[SC4] unexpected: Known-advisory checks are hard to verify without exact dependency versions; this supports user caution but does not by itself prove malicious behavior.\n[T09] unexpected: Static evidence confirms material implementation risks: arbitrary URL retrieval, remote filename path traversal on album downloads, insecure cookie output/storage, predictable temporary QR file use, and public-by-default album creation.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789177161414}}}}}